    "id": 1784003523746,
    "content": "**RMBGH Official Mailing System and Communication Policy**\n\n\n**1. Objective**\nThis policy defines the rules for using the Rosario Maclang Bautista General Hospital (RMBGH) electronic mail system. It ensures secure, professional, and legally compliant communication across all hospital operations.\n\n**2. Scope**\nThis policy applies to all employees, medical staff, contractors, and interns using official hospital email addresses (e.g., @quezoncity.gov.ph or official RMBGH subdomains).\n\n**3. Acceptable Use**\n- Business Purpose: Use hospital email strictly for official healthcare, administrative, and operational communications.\n- Professional Tone: Maintain a professional, polite, and clear tone in all messages.\n- Official Signatures: Include your full name, job title, department, and contact information in all outgoing emails.\n\n**4. Data Privacy and Confidentiality**\n- Patient Privacy: Never send Patient Health Information (PHI) to external or personal email addresses.\n- Encryption: Encrypt all emails containing sensitive medical records or financial details.No Auto-Forwarding: Do not set up automatic forwarding to personal email accounts (like Gmail or Yahoo).\n\n**5. Prohibited Activities**\n- Do not use hospital email for personal business, political campaigns, or commercial gain.\n- Do not distribute offensive, defamatory, or discriminatory material.\n- Do not share email passwords or allow unauthorized personnel to use your account.\n\n**6. Monitoring and Compliance**\nThe RMBGH IT Department monitors the mail system to protect network security.\nUsers have no expectation of privacy for messages sent or received on hospital networks.\nViolating this policy may lead to disciplinary action, including suspension or termination.",
